{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q214769","formula":"MgO","hill":"MgO","elements":["O","Mg"],"composition":{"O":1.0,"Mg":1.0},"names":{"en":"Magnesium oxide","ru":"Оксид магния","uk":"Оксид магнію"},"descriptions":{"en":"Magnesium oxide (MgO), or magnesia, is a white hygroscopic solid mineral that occurs naturally as periclase and is a source of magnesium (see also oxide). It has an empirical formula of MgO and consists of a lattice of Mg2+ ions and O2− ions held together by ionic bonding. Magnesium hydroxide forms in the presence of water (MgO + H2O → Mg(OH)2), but it can be reversed by heating it to remove moisture.","ru":"Окси́д ма́гния (жжёная магнезия) — химическое соединение с формулой MgO, белые кристаллы, малорастворимые в воде, пожаро- и взрывобезопасен. Относится к классу основных оксидов. Основная форма — минерал периклаз.","uk":"Окси́д ма́гнію (англ. magnesium oxide, нім. Magnesiumoxid) — оксид з формулою MgO. Складається з іонів Mg2+ та O2−, між якими діють іонні зв'язки."},"fame":60,"pubchemCid":14792,"mass":40.305,"charge":0,"smiles":"O=[Mg]","inchikey":"CPLXHLVBOLITMK-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"oxomagnesium","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-1265","atoms":27,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[4.194,0.0,0.0],[0.0,4.194,0.0],[0.0,0.0,4.194]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Mg"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":4.194,"el":"Mg"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.194,"z":0.0,"el":"Mg"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.194,"z":4.194,"el":"Mg"},{"x":4.194,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Mg"},{"x":4.194,"y":0.0,"z":4.194,"el":"Mg"},{"x":4.194,"y":4.194,"z":0.0,"el":"Mg"},{"x":4.194,"y":4.194,"z":4.194,"el":"Mg"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":2.097,"el":"O"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.194,"z":2.097,"el":"O"},{"x":4.194,"y":0.0,"z":2.097,"el":"O"},{"x":4.194,"y":4.194,"z":2.097,"el":"O"},{"x":0.0,"y":2.097,"z":2.097,"el